+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). Export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`; it
+returns the value the pointer refers to and throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer or does
+not resolve to a value of the document. Later features build on it.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- "" refers to the whole document; each `/`-separated token descends one level.
+- `~1` decodes to `/` and `~0` to `~` (in that order); any other `~` escape is invalid.
+- A non-empty pointer not starting with `/` is invalid.
+- Object members are looked up by own property only; arrays take only canonical indexes (`0` or no leading zeros, digits only); `-` and out-of-range indexes do not resolve.
+- Descending into a primitive or null does not resolve.
+- Tests in `test/pointer.test.ts` (`npm test`).
